# dircolors, light background variant. Monochrome.
#
# Derived from the dircolors file in this directory. File types are told
# apart by lightness and by attributes rather than by hue, on a ladder that
# runs dark to light against a #d4d4d4 ground:
#
#   237 bold  directories, the anchor      243  archives
#   (238      body text, uncoloured)       244  patches
#   241 bold  executables                  245  fifo, sock
#   242 under symbolic links               246  devices, libraries
#                                          247  backups, deliberately dim
#
# The dim end tracks the background: when the ground moved two steps
# darker, backups moved from 248 to 247 to hold the same separation.
#
# Colour is reserved for things that are wrong: broken links, core files,
# setuid and setgid. In an otherwise grey listing that is what makes them
# carry. Merely other-writable or sticky directories get reversed grey
# badges instead, since those are structural rather than alarming.
#
# Selected by theme light.

